title: The Last Thesis
subtitle: The debate turns on the clause about expulsions.
view-if: congress = 1 and congress_heidelberg = 1 and congress_closing = 0 and heid_cg_thesis = 0 and heid_motion <= 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.heid_cg_thesis = 1;
var sp = RG.speaker('luxemburgist');
Q.heid_speaker_name = sp.name;
Q.heid_speaker_power = sp.power;
RG.congress.tally();
!}
frequency: 400
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: congress

= The Last Thesis

On the second day the debate stops being about elections and becomes about the party itself. [? if heid_motion = 1 : Wolffheim says the last thesis is a guillotine with a footnote. ?][? if heid_motion = 2 : The Left Radicals say the missing thesis is still there, written in invisible ink. ?] The Right's delegates from Saxony ask whether a young party can afford to throw out half of itself. [+ heid_speaker_name +] is to answer for the Zentrale tonight.

[? if heid_natbol = 1 : The Zentrale has the Hamburg articles on a people's war against the Entente, with the officers' clubs' letters of thanks. ?]

- @firm: Answer them: a party is a discipline, or it is nothing.
- @drop: Drop the clause, and win the waverers.
- @restore: Put the clause back: name the splitters.
- @natbol: Read out the Hamburg articles.

@firm
subtitle: Our best speaker against their best. The Spartacists' line, and the hall will remember the speech.
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.sway(0.04 * Q.heid_speaker_power);
RG.congress.bitter(2);
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 3;
!}

[+ heid_speaker_name +] speaks for an hour and a half without a note. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates are won over before the end. ?][? if congress_last_moved = 0 : The hall applauds, and nobody changes sides. ?] Our side has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall.

@drop
view-if: heid_motion = 1
subtitle: The Right's advice. Easier to win, and the Left Radicals stay. The Zentrale's own people feel betrayed.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_motion = 2;
RG.congress.sway(0.07);
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 6;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 5;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
RG.ecci('radek', 4);
!}

The Zentrale withdraws the last thesis in the middle of the debate. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates who could not vote to expel their comrades can now vote with us. ?] Our side has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall. Some of our own delegates are not speaking to the Zentrale.

@restore
view-if: heid_motion = 2
subtitle: The Spartacists will be glad. The waverers will not.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_motion = 1;
RG.congress.lose(0.05);
RG.congress.bitter(4);
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
!}

The clause goes back into the theses, with the names of the districts it means. Our side now has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall, and the Left Radicals know exactly where they stand.

@natbol
view-if: heid_natbol = 1
subtitle: Turns the debate on Laufenberg and Wolffheim. Bremen, which dislikes their nationalism, may break away from Hamburg.
on-arrival: {!
var n = RG.congress.convert('bremen', 0.35) + RG.congress.convert('berlin', 0.1);
RG.congress.tally();
Q.congress_last_moved = n;
RG.congress.bitter(3);
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 5;
!}

The Hamburg articles are read aloud, slowly, with the officers' letters after them. The Bremen delegates go out to confer, and come back divided. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates come over to us. ?] Our side has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall.
